<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs exclusions for the `analyze` profile (pom.xml, ARCHITECTURE.md §3.2).

  Every entry says why. An exclusion without a reason is a finding that was switched off rather
  than answered, and the next person cannot tell the two apart. Anything not listed here is a
  finding this project intends to fix, and the gate is red until it is.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>

  <!--
    EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2: records and small classes that hold a byte[] hand it back
    without copying.

    This is deliberate, and for the key material it is the safer of the two options. A defensive
    copy of a private key, a Noise cipher state or a handshake transcript does not protect it: it
    puts a second copy in the heap that nobody owns, nobody wipes, and that outlives the one
    `Arrays.fill` clears. The crypto module wipes what it holds (`CipherState.destroy`,
    `Blake2s.digest`), and a copy defeats exactly that.

    The wider argument is that none of these types is public API. crypto, proto, node and hub are
    four modules of one program that ship as two binaries; there is no caller outside this
    repository to defend against, only code in this repository, which the tests cover.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Blake2s.digest: `(byte) (h[i >>> 2] >>> (8 * (i & 3)))`. SpotBugs warns that an unsigned shift
    feeding a byte cast is usually a mistake. Here it cannot be: the cast keeps the low 8 bits, and
    `>>>` and `>>` differ only above them, so the two spellings produce identical bytes for every
    input. The RFC 7693 vectors in Blake2sTest pin the output either way.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.crypto.Blake2s"/>
    <Method name="digest"/>
    <Bug pattern="ICAST_QUESTIONABLE_UNSIGNED_RIGHT_SHIFT"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Store.load and Hub.start: fields written during construction and startup, read under a lock
    afterwards. `load` is called from the Store constructor, before any reference to the object has
    escaped, so there is no second thread to race with; `Hub.start` runs once before the accept
    loop exists. SpotBugs counts accesses, not lifetimes, so it sees 75% and 80% and cannot see
    that the other 20% is single-threaded by construction.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.hub.Store"/>
    <Field name="~(eventsSinceSnapshot|nextNodeId)"/>
    <Bug pattern="IS2_INCONSISTENT_SYNC"/>
  </Match>
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.hub.Hub"/>
    <Field name="~(acme|timer)"/>
    <Bug pattern="IS2_INCONSISTENT_SYNC"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Tls.PROTOCOLS / TLS13_ONLY / ALPN_HTTP11 and Tls13.CERT_VERIFY_CONTEXT are constant arrays.
    Java has no immutable array, and the alternative — a List copied to an array at each use,
    allocates on the TLS handshake path to protect against code in this repository editing its own
    constants. Same argument as EI_EXPOSE_REP above: there is no caller outside the repository.
    DnsQuery.PUBLIC_RESOLVERS was the one worth changing and is now a List, because which
    resolvers validate the hub's own DNS is a security decision (§7.2) rather than a wire constant.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Or>
      <Class name="io.jailscale.proto.tls.Tls"/>
      <Class name="io.jailscale.proto.tls.Tls13"/>
    </Or>
    <Bug pattern="MS_PKGPROTECT,MS_MUTABLE_ARRAY,MS_EXPOSE_REP"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Log.setOutput stores the caller's PrintStream in a static field. That is what the method is
    for: tests redirect the log, and `jailhub`/`jailscale` point it at stderr. Copying a stream is
    not a thing one can do.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.proto.util.Log"/>
    <Method name="setOutput"/>
    <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_STATIC_REP2"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    RemoteSigning.RecordingRandom and RemotePrivateKey carry `serialVersionUID` and transient
    fields because SecureRandom and PrivateKey are Serializable, not because either is ever
    serialised. A RemotePrivateKey holds no key bytes to restore (that is the point, §9.2) and
    serialising one would be meaningless; there is no writeObject anywhere in the project.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="~io\.jailscale\.node\.RemoteSigning\$.*"/>
    <Bug pattern="SE_TRANSIENT_FIELD_NOT_RESTORED,SE_BAD_FIELD,SE_NO_SERIALVERSIONID"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Service writes launchd plists and systemd units, where the line terminator is LF on every
    platform the file is read on. `%n` would emit CRLF when the CLI happens to run on Windows and
    produce a unit file systemd rejects. The literal "\n" is the correct one here.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.node.Service"/>
    <Bug pattern="VA_FORMAT_STRING_USES_NEWLINE"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Path.getParent() can return null for a single-element relative path, which is the null path
    SpotBugs is following. Every one of these parents is a directory the caller already resolved
    against a state or config directory (`dir.resolve("node.json").getParent()` is `dir`), so the
    null case needs a path with no directory part, which none of these can be handed.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Bug pattern="NP_NULL_ON_SOME_PATH_FROM_RETURN_VALUE"/>
    <Or>
      <Class name="io.jailscale.proto.acme.AcmeKeys"/>
      <Class name="io.jailscale.proto.ipc.Ipc"/>
      <Class name="io.jailscale.node.NodeState"/>
      <Class name="io.jailscale.node.Service"/>
    </Or>
  </Match>

  <!--
    Hub's hand-off path calls System.exit: the old process has handed its listeners over and has
    nothing left to do, and it must not run shutdown hooks that would delete the new process's
    socket (§13). A CLI ending itself on purpose is not the bug this pattern is about.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.hub.Hub"/>
    <Bug pattern="DM_EXIT"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    HubConfig's default state directory is /var/lib/jailhub, which is documented in §6.2 and
    overridden by $JAILHUB_STATE or by the state flag on the command line. A default has to be written down somewhere.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.jailscale.hub.HubConfig"/>
    <Bug pattern="DMI_HARDCODED_ABSOLUTE_FILENAME"/>
  </Match>

  <!--
    A redundant null check on a value SpotBugs proved non-null. Harmless, and the check documents
    the JCE contract that engineSign may be reached without a key.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="~io\.jailscale\.node\.RemoteSigning\$.*"/>
    <Bug pattern="RCN_REDUNDANT_NULLCHECK_OF_NONNULL_VALUE"/>
  </Match>

</FindBugsFilter>
